  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "The second family",
     "texto": [
      "The other type of adjective behaves like a noun. They are called **-na** adjectives because they take **な** when they go before a noun: **しずか な まち** (quiet town), **ゆうめい な こうえん** (famous park).",
      "At the end of the sentence they don't take な: **この まち は しずか です** (this town is quiet).",
      "They are negated like nouns: **しずか じゃ ありません** (it is not quiet)."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "tabla",
     "titulo": "-na adjectives",
     "columnas": [
      {
       "texto": "Use",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "Japanese",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      },
      {
       "texto": "English",
       "lengua": "alumno"
      }
     ],
     "filas": [
